Sam Taylor
Example: fall at work (made up)
1 June 2026
What happened
When and where
1 February 2026 · 14:20 · Loading bay, Northgate Distribution, Leeds
Beforehand
I was unloading pallets at the end of a normal shift.
What happened
A pallet slipped off the forklift and knocked me down. I landed on my right wrist and hit my head on the kerb.
What happened next
A first aider stayed with me and my supervisor called an ambulance. I was taken to Leeds General Infirmary.
Complications
The wrist needed an operation to fix it with a plate two weeks later.
What I was told at the time
The paramedic said I might have broken my wrist and should not drive.
Other people there
Priya from the day shift, and my supervisor Dan.
Police, ambulance or fire service
Ambulance. The incident was logged in the accident book.
Treatment and medication
Straight afterwards
X-ray, a plaster cast and painkillers in A&E.
Ongoing care
Physiotherapy weekly, and fracture clinic every six weeks.
